  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2026 LB4075 Lebanon Acute Crisis Joint Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The crisis disproportionately impacts the most vulnerable households, which includes (domestic) migrant workers, and non-Lebanese refugees who have been reported to have limited access to shelters and distributions. The primary beneficiaries are Internally Displaced People (IDPs), specifically new IDPs pertaining to the recent developments from March 2nd on. People left behind, vulnerable Households (HHs) (elderly people, people with disabilities (PWDs) who could not evacuate, children) and the host communities of the new IDPs are also a priority target group. Finally, Syrian and Palestinian refugees are to be prioritised as well, due to their potential struggle to access government-issued aid and support. Areas of support include: Food Security &amp; Livelihoods, Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance, WASH, Health and Protection.</narrative>
  </description>
